# Consumer infrared (IR) transmitter
#
# The IR HAL (android.hardware.ir@1.0-service, domain hal_ir_default)
# drives the LGE "sdc_spi_ir" SPI IR driver through its sysfs
# attributes.  The CAF blob consumerir.msm8952.so opens
#
#   /sys/class/spi_master/spi6/spi6.0/ir_data
#
# and writes the carrier/modulation pattern into it; the framework then
# reports "ConsumerIrService: Error transmitting: -1" when the open
# fails, because the blob logs "Can't open sysfs file ...".
#
# AOSP gives hal_ir_default no access to sysfs at all
# (system/sepolicy/public/hal_ir.te only covers the HIDL binder calls),
# so the HAL was never allowed to open the node and no IR signal was
# emitted at all.
#
# The two attributes carry their own type (sysfs_ir, see sepolicy/file.te
# and sepolicy/genfs_contexts) so that the permission stays limited to
# the IR interface instead of opening up all of sysfs for the HAL.
allow hal_ir_default sysfs_ir:file { getattr open read write };

# The HAL runs as the "system" user, and the driver creates the
# attributes as root:root 0660, so init has to hand them over - see
# rootdir/etc/init.target.rc.  init already has setattr on the sysfs
# attributes through
#   allow init { fs_type -contextmount_type -sdcard_type -rootfs }:file
#          { open read setattr };
# (system/sepolicy/public/init.te), no extra rule is needed for that.
